  },
  data: {
    LLM: '1. Before deal: Each player contributes 1 chip to the pool\n2. Deal: 13 cards to each player\n3. If a player has four of a kind: No play occurs; highest four of a kind wins all 4 chips\n4. Otherwise: Players sort hands into up to four 3-card combinations\n5. Discard face down any cards not part of valid combinations (each card used in only one combination)\n6. Showdowns occur in order: strongest combination first, then second strongest, etc.\n7. Winner of each showdown takes 1 chip from the pool',
    Player: '1. Before deal: Each player contributes 1 chip to the pool\n2. Deal: 13 cards to each player\n3. If a player has four of a kind: No play occurs; highest four of a kind wins all 4 chips\n4. Otherwise: Players sort hands into up to four 3-card combinations\n5. Discard face down any cards not part of valid combinations (each card used in only one combination)\n6. Showdowns occur in order: strongest combination first, then second strongest, etc.\n7. Winner of each showdown takes 1 chip from the pool',
    objective: 'Win chips from the pool by forming stronger 3-card combinations than opponents. The player with the highest four of a kind (if dealt) wins all four chips immediately.',
    gameplay: '1. Before deal: Each player contributes 1 chip to the pool\n2. Deal: 13 cards to each player\n3. If a player has four of a kind: No play occurs; highest four of a kind wins all 4 chips\n4. Otherwise: Players sort hands into up to four 3-card combinations\n5. Discard face down any cards not part of valid combinations (each card used in only one combination)\n6. Showdowns occur in order: strongest combination first, then second strongest, etc.\n7. Winner of each showdown takes 1 chip from the pool',
    keyRules: [
      'Three-card combinations rank (high to low): Three of a kind, Running flush (3-card straight flush), Run (3-card straight), Flush (3 cards same suit), Three unrelated cards',
      "Three unrelated cards must have no suit connection and no pair - if two cards share a suit or form a pair, they cannot be 'unrelated'",
      'Each card can only be used in one combination',
      'Unused cards are discarded face down and do not play',
      'Four of a kind ends the hand immediately with that player winning',
      'Combinations compared using standard Brag hand rankings',
